  "Question": "A and B are 100 km apart and travel toward each other at speeds of 30 and 20 km/h. After how many hours will they meet? (Unit: hours)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For a meeting problem, the sum of the distances equals the sum of the speeds multiplied by the time. Thus, \\((30+20)t=100\\), so \\(t=2\\).",
